My second ascension, and a very educational experience!

I'm naming characters after elements.  My first ascension, Carbon (wiz), is 
6th in the periodic table.  Thallium is 81st.  Its now apparent just how 
much of a cakewalk the first one was.  I played all combat-wombat this time. 
What broke this game open was finding wizard bones.

Notables:
Couldn't get Excalibur.  I dried up every fountain above Gehennom trying 
(except for some potion dipping).  Unless it was sitting in a hidden closet, 
I don't know how I didn't get it, as my luck was high.  It eventually didn't 
matter, as Mojo is plenty of weapon.

Relied heavily on price ID of items and tracked it all in a spreadsheet. 
Had all potions, scrolls, and wands IDed before the Castle.

Got 2 touchstones out of the mines and holy water in a shop, and cleaned out 
the general stores by selling them gems and having my pets steal them back 
(nice shiny objects!).  Could see how much cash they had left and leave them 
just enough to price ID for me.

Tried to go !geno, but got really bogged down by arch-liches on the 
ascension run.  I finally got sick of all the cursing and summoning and 
whipped out my scroll of blessed genocide.

Tyr was kind of stingy, except for Mjollnir.  I once used 7 cursed scrolls 
of create monster at his altar, and got one four-leaf clover and 
Snickersnee.  7 black unicorns sacrificed (from reverse genocide) only got 
me a celestial atta-boy.  Tyr wouldn't crown me, even with the Amulet.  I 
got 1 point of protection, and my long sword blessed out of two tries.

Game story:
I picked a dwarf race so I would have more peace in the mines.  Went 
straight in and found 3 types of gray stones I could kick.  Cold, fire, and 
shock resistance early, but poison took a long time.  Minetown altar was 
cross-aligned, and I had no cash for protection.  No sacks of any kind so 
far, so I retreated to find one and some cash.  Altar on DL3 and plenty of 
shops to price ID.  Found holy water, IDed and blessed up the touchstones 
and luckstone, and ran the gem scam.  Got Rhodium the Priest's bones on DL8, 
but not much there.  Sokoban had the amulet level, so I abandoned it to 
continue my sack hunt.  I had finally realized to do Sokoban with blind 
telepathy (infravision from being a dwarf helped) to see monsters spawn 
behind boulders.  Finally got lucky with Fluorine the Wizard's bones on 
DL13.  Blessed BoH and a CoMR.  Back to Sokoban for reflection.  I left my 
pets behind for this.  I had stealth from elven boots, so I was able to 
clear the zoo quietly and leave the white unicorn and the incubus alone in 
the no-teleport zone.  Maxed out my luck and gained a couple of levels. 
Camped in the Elbereth closet while waiting for the incubus to get back in 
the mood.

Finally got poison resistance and headed down to Minetown to buy 5 points of 
protection.  Cleared the bottom for the gems and got a glass golem and 
skeleton from the poly traps.  They turned out to be pretty tough pets, and 
the skeleton wielded a dwarvish mattock.  They made short work of the 
shopkeepers in Minetown (except Izchak, I locked his door), and I got 2 more 
points protection from their cash.  My pets did the same to a large potion 
shop and deli in the main dungeon, and I got yet 2 more points protection. 
Unfortunately, a purple worm ate my skeleton.

I converted the altar on DL3 and got Mjollnir on saccing an ogre.  My main 
weapon for the rest of the game.  Made a stash on DL17 and went on the 
quest.  Found two wands of death so Lord Surtur was toast.  Lots of strength 
and gems from the fire giants.  The Orb of Fate is a good artifact.  Half 
physical and magic damage was really valuable.  With good armor and HP, 
you're close to unkillable. (By monsters)

Medusa was easy, froze the swamp and went in blind and reflective.  No 
messing around with the castle drawbridge this time.  Took my storming kit, 
got in safe and cleared it out.  Used the WoW to armor up and get a magic 
marker, and went back to the stash for some polypiling, enchanting, and 
alchemy.  Best results were a ring of levitation and a silver saber.  I 
tried to polymorph a tame glass piercer and it shuddered and died (why?), 
Tyr pissed off.  Polyselfed to a xorn and ate a ring of increase damage. 
Converted another altar on DL20, sacfested, but couldn't get crowned. 
Whatever.  Kerry the white dragon and I hit the trapdoor for Gehennom.

Gehennom was really tedious, but no threat.  AC of -40, twoweaponing with +7 
Mojo and +7 silver saber.  LOTS of full/extra heal potions laying around and 
in death drops.  That and a few nurses got HP up to over 400.  Paid off 
Asmodeus and Baalzebub, Juiblex and Yeenoghu and Orcus went down easy.  Only 
red alert moment was while nurse dancing in Orcus town, and an arch-lich 
pops up and summons a horde.  After I get dressed and wipe them out, I find 
holy water in the death drop (!), and a peaceful djinni.  Kerry in now a 
wumpus.  Vlad was cake, got the candelabraum, but I'm burdened now. 
Vibrating square on DL48, mark it and go for the Wizard's tower.  Ring of 
conflict all the way in the tower, deathray the smart-ass Rodney and get the 
Book of the Dead.  Big arch-lich trouble in the bottom of the tower, cursed 
my BoH and gremlins multiplying in the moat.  I finally get my stuff 
uncursed and blessed, wipe out the horde, and invoke the Orb to level tele 
to the VS level.  Do the invocation, fight thru the graveyard, and have to 
take on both Rodney and the high priest of Moloch in the sanctum.  Had to 
deathray the priest.  Got the AoY, name it real, and cused gain level thru 
the ceiling.  Grab Kerry, who is now an ice devil (useful in Gehennom), and 
get out of there.  Had to genocide L when the arch-liches got to be too 
much; it was starting to look like Astral in there, and I wanted to save my 
teleport wands.

Out of Gehennom, grab my gem and artifact stash, fail to get crowned again, 
an dgo to trim pack.  I bless up a magic lamp from Gehennom, get a wish, and 
the blessed figurine of an Archon makes a peaceful, but untamable monster. 
Oh well, I leave for the planes with a jabberwock, yellow dragon, black 
dragon, and ice devil.  Snooped the portals with the Orb of Fate.  Earth was 
easy.  Air was harder, and I lost all my pets (3 died, one still eating when 
I hit the portal).  Fire was a tedious runaway from everything.  Water 
wasn't bad, the portal showed up quickly.

Astral was a mess.  Never again will I show up there burdened.  Death left, 
Famine middle, Pestilence right.  My guardian angel kills off a player 
character, and I scoop up a bunch of gems.  Put on ring of slow digestion 
and head up the middle.  It doesn't help as much as I thought, because 
Famine still makes me hungry.  Deathray him, then Gregg the Rogue beheads me 
with Vorpal Blade!  But wait...the "oLS saves me...whew!  I can't seem to 
kill him, so I teleport everyone away long enought to get to the altar. 
Chaotic!  Head back out to the foyer and Famine shrivels me again.  Deathray 
him again and I kill a peaceful priestess of Tyr on the rebound.  You 
murderer!  The Angel of Tyr then opens up on me, vowing to make me pay for 
my insolence.  Curses, hordes, spells, and I'm stressed from a hit on my 
BoH.  I finally bless that up and pull out my stack of blessed full heals to 
recover the 150HP and all but one are blown up by a fire spell.  Quaff the 
remaining one and teleport a path to the hall.  My Guardian Angel of Tyr is 
taking on the Angel of Tyr, what loyalty!  And he pays for it with his life 
:-(  On goes the ring of conflict :-)  Pestilence sickens me, and my trusty 
unihorn cures me.  Deathray for him.  Much easier to get thru the mob when 
they are fighting each other.  I take the opportunity to kill Gregg the 
Rogue and take Vorpal Blade off his corpse.  Bull my way to the altar and 
its lawful!  Tyr,  I would really rather don a helm of OA and give this to 
Loki, but here it is...

